        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_34.lnote.oe.6-3" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">publicis gemotibus</hi> (<hi rend="italic">ohne</hi> co. te.) <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> alia terra in pu. co. te. puplicis gemotibus <hi rend="italic">Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">publicis gemotibus</hi> (without co. te.) K; alia terra in pu. co. te. puplicis gemotibus Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_34.lnote.oe.7-3" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> g. <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> conu. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only g. Lond; only conu. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_34.lnote.oe.8-3" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sic s. s. o. sit <hi rend="italic">nur Lond, fehlt übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic s. s. o. sit only Lond, lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_34.lnote.oe.1-4" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þæt <hi rend="italic">später eingefügt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þæt inserted later</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_34.lnote.oe.2-4" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geändert</hi> lædað</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to lædað</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_34.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> ma manna</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply ma manna</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_34.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Handel 8b—e; Stadt 2. 15; Markt 2a. 7. Spät noch <hi rend="italic">mercatores residere debent in villis de burgh et non upland;</hi> a. 1341; Gross <hi rend="italic">Gild merch.</hi> II 358</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Handel 8b—e; Stadt 2. 15; Markt 2a. 7. Still at a late date: <hi rend="italic">mercatores residere debent in villis de burgh et non upland;</hi> a. 1341; Gross <hi rend="italic">Gild merch.</hi> II 358</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_34.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Das ordentliche staatliche Gericht (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4f) des Bezirks, dem der staatliche Vogt (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 6) vorsitzt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The regular state court (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4f) of the district, presided over by the state reeve (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 6)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_34.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ellipse (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Wb</hi>) des Subjekts. Q ändert hier und in <hi rend="italic">notificent</hi> den Sg. in Pl. und denkt hinzu: ‘die Kaufleute’. Sinnesgleich ‘der Unternehmer’ ist vielleicht schon hier richtig, denn nur dies passt für <hi rend="italic">gecyðe</hi> 4 Z. weiter. Af schwankt also zwischen den Numeri, bald an den Führer allein, bald an die Handelsgesellschaft denkend. Doch könnte zu <hi rend="italic">gerecce,</hi> wie sonst oft, hier auch ‘Vogt’ oder ‘Gericht’ Subjekt sein. — Schreiber H versucht teilweise, in <hi rend="italic">gebringe</hi>⁵, zu normalisieren.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ellipsis (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi>) of the subject. Q changes the sg. to the pl. here and in <hi rend="italic">notificent</hi>, and understands ‘the merchants’. ‘The entrepreneur’, which amounts to the same sense, is perhaps already correct here, for only this fits <hi rend="italic">gecyðe</hi> 4 ll. further on. Af thus wavers between the numbers, thinking now of the leader alone, now of the trading company. Yet with <hi rend="italic">gerecce,</hi> as often elsewhere, ‘reeve’ or ‘court’ could here also be the subject. — Scribe H attempts in part, in <hi rend="italic">gebringe</hi>⁵, to normalize.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_34.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Fremde Gehilfen, nicht einheimische Geleitsmänner (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi>), für die die folgende Kautel nicht nötig wäre, und die der Reisende auch nicht in Mehrzahl brauchte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Foreign assistants, not native escorts (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi>), for whom the following precaution would not be necessary, and of whom the traveller would not need several either</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_34.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Oder ‘zum Gericht zum Prozesse’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Or ‘to the court for the lawsuit’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_34.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Gen. part. hinter Komparativ. — Auch hier hat Lambarde nicht B allein benutzt, da er das von B Übersehene bringt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Partitive gen. after a comparative. — Here too Lambarde did not use B alone, since he gives what B overlooked</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_34.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o.</hi> Erkl. 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> note 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_34.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">57</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Durch Gleichklang verführt setzt Q öfter falsch <hi rend="italic">simul; s. Wb.</hi> Die letzten 5 Wörter bewahrt nur Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi>. — ‘Im Zeugnis’ = ‘unter behördlicher Aufsicht, Erlaubnis’ auch Af 37. 37, 1. 41; Ine 3, 1¹</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Misled by the similarity of sound, Q often wrongly puts <hi rend="italic">simul; see Wb.</hi> Only Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> preserves the last 5 words. — ‘In witness’ = ‘under official supervision, with official permission’ also Af 37. 37, 1. 41; Ine 3, 1¹</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_34.attnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope></bibl><label>ða</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þæt ða</hi>. B.</seg></note>
